# N0: status of the four-card set, an all-four reset with the heal, then build the tp4-next-1 image (the tp4/next head: tp4/stack-fix
# (speed slide, exact per-tile collectives, quad draft, the prefill warm before every capture), tp4/fcommit (fused commit, live banks),
# tp4/vglue (five verify levers) and the lanes work). The build opens no card; the reset first means a card, link or hugepage fault
# fails here, before the smokes. Run first.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image N0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built
# from the pushed branch; the driver's IMAGE_TAG env overrides it.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock): status 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 min (up to 12); build 7-15 min with the layers cached, 30-70 min
# cold (step limit 75). Typical 18 min, at most 90. It runs the image copy-closure and overlay tests first and tags the image only if
# they pass, so a closure error fails here with no card touched. Check df on the rig first: a new image is about 32 GB.
# Read: the status listing (four boards, one firmware bundle, at least 4 free 1 GiB hugepages, no holders, no platform serving
# container, disk); the build log (closure tests OK, provenance passed, the vglue and fused-commit sources in the image).
# STOP on any failure.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best
